From 713c99fb5cb10511e0eb0777d5797d0878552885 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 02:23:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Filter the CRM customer view to designs linked to that
 customer, and add a staff lookup
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

crm.deal returned the customer directory, which lists every design owned by
the merged person, so opening a customer showed every saved design on the
account. Add crm.customerDesigns, which filters server-side on the stored link:
crm_deal_designs for the deal and kitchen_designs.contractorCustomerId for the
deal's contractor customer folder. No link means an empty list, never a guess.

Add crm.customerLookup for the phone-call case: staff type the customer number
(crm_deals.id) and get that customer's linked designs — one opens straight
away, several are offered to pick from, none says so. The identifier is parsed
and matched on the deal row inside the caller's scope; it is never a search
across designs, and a ?customer= link (a users.id) is refused rather than
matched against a different number space.

A linked design is returned with its OWN store slug rather than being filtered
by the deal's store, so the client builds the Designer link from the design,
matching main's #274 rule that a saved design opens under the store that owns
it.

Also make the in-memory test store honour a multi-value IN predicate, which a
two-id inArray produces.
